From 8832cf2d2368dc666a82b3d15fb3efc6123da744 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Grahmann <lars.grahmann@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:25:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] synaptics_tudor: Add TLS client and pairing certificates

The Tudor sensors speak a bent TLS 1.2 (ECDH-ECDSA with AES-256-GCM,
no extensions length, no compression methods, fixed size signatures)
and want a host certificate signed by a fixed key at pairing time.
Everything is built on OpenSSL EVP and has no USB in it.
---
 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor.h     |   89 ++
 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor_tls.c | 1040 +++++++++++++++++
 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor_tls.h |   77 ++
 3 files changed, 1206 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor.h
 create mode 100644 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor_tls.c
 create mode 100644 libfprint/drivers/synaptics_tudor/tudor_tls.h

